codex
The merge path has a second, independent integrity gap: it proves the branch still points at the declared commit, but the reviewers are given the database’s text result rather than the bytes from that commit. A builder can therefore make the declaration and the branch agree while supplying benign text to reviewers. I’m validating whether any caller reconstructs the review bundle from Git; so far, none does.
